.TH KIDSH 1 "August 2026" "kidsh" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kidsh \- lightweight secure shell for young children
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kidsh
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kidsh
(Kid Shell) is a lightweight, low-capability shell for young children
to explore a computer safely. It offers simple built-in commands for
easy tasks, such as showing colors or days of the week, or taking notes.
It is meant to run in a dedicated full-screen terminal so children cannot
easily leave the environment.
.PP
Built-in commands are not listed in this manual page; they can change
independently of the packaged documentation. While the shell is running,
type
.B help
for the current list.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose output.
.TP
.B \-e
Exit on error.
.TP
.B \-n
Dry-run; do not execute commands.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR help " (" helpme ", " cmds ")"
Print every built-in command, its aliases, and a short description.
.TP
.BR quit " (" exit ")"
Leave the shell.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Optional JSON configuration is read from the first readable file among:
.IP \(bu 2
the path in the
.B KIDSH_CONFIG
environment variable, if set
.IP \(bu 2
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kidsh/config.json ,
or
.I ~/.config/kidsh/config.json
if
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset
.IP \(bu 2
.I $SNAP/etc/kidsh.json
when running as a Snap
.IP \(bu 2
.I /etc/kidsh.json
.IP \(bu 2
.I /etc/kidsh/config.json
.PP
Packages also ship this example as
.I kidsh.json.example
in the documentation directory (typically
.IR /usr/share/doc/kidsh/ ):
.PP
.nf
.RS
{
  "rssUrl": "",
  "contactsVcfFile": "",
  "familyInfoFile": "",
  "bedtimeHour": 21,
  "bedtimeMinute": 0,
  "blacklistedCommands": [],
  "todoFile": "",
  "myName": "",
  "weatherUrl": ""
}
.RE
.fi
.PP
The
.B myName
setting is significant. It is important to set this name to the name used for
the user in the
.B contactsVcfFile
match so that shell commands can know who the user is.
.PP
The
.B weatherUrl
setting is the URL of a weather service that runs
.UR https://github.com/schachmat/wego
.UE
\&.
An example is
.UR https://wttr.in/St.%20Johns,%20Florida?format=3&u
.UE
\&.
.SH NOTES
The interface is English only. Output uses ANSI escape sequences for
colors; a color-capable terminal is expected.
